Subject: [PATCH] vayu camera S1/S3: the stills mode's first frame exposed from the usual mode's AE, and a per-100-frame preview timing line

Base (kernel): the shared merge-all tree, bsd/dev/vayu_camera.c sha256
537024ea776cfb812aeb9fbf45184547a613dfc52314b8e7236cb225c6692b86 (vayu-test26 + cam31).
Base (userland): work/hkd-ws20/userland/src/camera_device.c =
/mnt/ramdisk/ds-ui/userland/src/camera_device.c, sha256
b3d92562bb61b3e04ec8e7b3bdba6f9c196850ca60a0d35b0b0d9e1017925f21 (the tree root-cam2 was
rebuilt from).

S1 (verification): cam_preview_half= and cam_neon= already default to 1 in camera_device.c
(boot_number(..., 1)); work/hkd-ws20's and hackios-vayu's copies are byte-identical. root-ui1's
cam_preview_half=0 came from an older build, not from this source. libhakios.media.dylib is
rebuilt from this source for root-cam3. Added: a line every 100 frames with isp_measure's time
and each preview output's render_piece() time (PrimaryScaler, SecondaryScaler), averaged since
the previous line.

S3: in mode 1 (the vendor's res1 block) the kernel wrote none of 0x0202/0x0204, and the vendor
block's own 0x0202 is 11 lines (0.12 ms), so the first stills frame was black and
cam_still_settle dropped two frames after it. cam_real_start() now hands cam_stream_up() the
usual mode's last AE exposure and gain; cam_stream_up() writes 0x0202 = the usual lines scaled
to the stills mode's line time (rear 13190 -> 10903 ns, front 8375 -> 16080 ns, computed from
the vendor 0x0340 and the mode's fps), clamped to the vendor frame less the row's margin, and
0x0204 = the usual gain's code, BEFORE the on block. 0x0340 stays the vendor block's (frame
length and frame rate unchanged). cam_still_settle defaults to 0, and the userland logs the
first stills frame's exposure/gain/green so one run proves it.

No boot-arg changes: the new behaviour is the default; cam_still_settle=N (0..10) still drops
the first N stills-mode frames.

